message: "If you use or reference this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "BrittleBench: A Defender's Audit of Public Detection Content Robustness"
abstract: >
  A large-scale empirical study measuring how robust publicly-published detection
  rules are when faced with LLM-generated functional mutations of the attacks
  those rules are designed to detect. Confirmatory Phase 1 is scoped to native
  YARA, native Elastic, and high-fidelity Sigma-to-Elastic rules. Produces a
  benchmark dataset, an open-source toolkit, and a primary publication.
